    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4e7f41e_3c71277d",
        "filename": "common/ap_hang_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1442602
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-11T12:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree - that could lead to the boot loop. What minimum timeout do you suggest? ( I was thinking about 5 or 10 sec)",
      "parentUuid": "5f290590_4e04046b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "77ffae066b7d137b72bca1786641a91de4d08fb7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e939f86_5f6495b1",
        "filename": "common/ap_hang_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-12T17:28:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a reboot is triggered, there will be no deferred call scheduled. So, I don\u0027t think reboot will loop. I think Keith\u0027s concern is triggering a reboot immediately after setting reboot_timeout_sec to ~0.\n\nI can\u0027t think of a reason we must reject reboot_timeout_sec\u003d0 but I think it\u0027s nice to do so.",
      "parentUuid": "c4e7f41e_3c71277d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "77ffae066b7d137b72bca1786641a91de4d08fb7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "241c545c_1e0b94bf",
        "filename": "common/ap_hang_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1442602
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-13T10:03:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes after a reboot the whole mechanism turns off, but when kernel boots and configures the reboot_timeout to 0s it will loop.\n\nI can imagine a following scenario:\n1. In userspace user set reboot_timeout\u003d0; \n2. Starts the watchdog which immediately reboots the borad (due to 0s timeout)\n3. Board boots, daisydog is automatically started  (as a service) and setups previously configured reboot_timeout\u003d0s what immediately restart the board.\n5. goto 3.\n\n\nI can think here of 2 solutions:\n1. Minimum reboot_timeout \n2. Fixed \"first timeout after boot\" - eg. when kernel boots and request a desired timeout (eg. 0) EC will ignore the first request and set the first \"timeout\" to e.g. 60 seconds, the next calls to hang_detect_reload() will use the requested (by kernel and user) timeout.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "7e939f86_5f6495b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "77ffae066b7d137b72bca1786641a91de4d08fb7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
